{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558533-horrid-reality","id":1558533,"title":"horrid reality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-26T12:38:32-08:00","id":1558533,"title":"horrid reality","content":"Does the target of horrid reality get a save to unbelieve the ilusion if its clearly supernatural or do only other people can convince him of that?<br /> VDA20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-27T00:52:51-08:00","id":1558545,"title":"","content":"By default:<br /> <br /> &quot;Mortals and vampires alike fall prey to these illusions unless<br /> the vampire has learned in sufficient levels of Auspex (see<br /> p. 195). Victims of Chimerstry can see through the illusions<br /> if they can \u201cprove\u201d the illusion\u2019s falsehood (e.g. a person<br /> who attempts to lean against an illusionary wall and passes<br /> through will no longer see the wall at all), and incredible<br /> illusions (e.g. monsters rising from the sea, or flying horses)<br /> give a chance for the victim to realize their falsehood with<br /> a roll of Perception + Alertness (difficulty 6).&quot;<br /> <br /> But<br /> The power clearly states:<br /> <br /> &quot;The illusion is so real that <b><i>the victim believes completely in its reality</i></b>&quot;<br /> <br /> So kind of &quot;overwrites&quot; as per written the default<br /> <br /> Also states:<br /> &quot;The victim can escape the terror of the Horrid Reality if he can be convinced the illusion is not real.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> So I would say - an this is how I treat it - <b>If</b> the victim can't catch the Horrid Reality is false upon its conjuration like with Auspex or other supernatural means or it is too unbelivable (and this is a bit murky, since the rising of a Demon or a Dragon or descending of the Archangel Uriel in the Dark Ages is not that &quot;unbelivable&quot; for example) with a Perception + Alertness (difficulty 6) check, <i>then</i> they only could escape if someone else saves them\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-27T00:53:42-08:00","id":1558546,"title":"","content":"Forum ate the edit, lets try this again....<br /> <br /> <br /> By default:<br /> <br /> &quot;Mortals and vampires alike fall prey to these illusions unless<br /> the vampire has learned in sufficient levels of Auspex (see<br /> p. 195). Victims of Chimerstry can see through the illusions<br /> if they can \u201cprove\u201d the illusion\u2019s falsehood (e.g. a person<br /> who attempts to lean against an illusionary wall and passes<br /> through will no longer see the wall at all), and incredible<br /> illusions (e.g. monsters rising from the sea, or flying horses)<br /> give a chance for the victim to realize their falsehood with<br /> a roll of Perception + Alertness (difficulty 6).&quot;<br /> <br /> But<br /> The power clearly states:<br /> <br /> &quot;The illusion is so real that <b><i>the victim believes completely in its reality</i></b>&quot;<br /> <br /> So kind of &quot;overwrites&quot; as per written the default<br /> <br /> Also states:<br /> &quot;The victim can escape the terror of the Horrid Reality if he can be convinced the illusion is not real.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> So I would say - an this is how I treat it - <b>If</b> the victim can't catch the Horrid Reality is false upon its conjuration like with Auspex or other supernatural means or it is too unbelivable (and this is a bit murky, since the rising of a Demon or a Dragon or descending of the Archangel Uriel in the Dark Ages is not that &quot;unbelivable&quot; for example) with a Perception + Alertness (difficulty 6) check, <i>then</i> they only could escape if someone else saves them\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T04:19:59-07:00","id":1561967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558533-horrid-reality?p=1558546#post1558546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I would say - an this is how I treat it - <b>If</b> the victim can't catch the Horrid Reality is false upon its conjuration like with Auspex or other supernatural means or it is too unbelivable (and this is a bit murky, since the rising of a Demon or a Dragon or descending of the Archangel Uriel in the Dark Ages is not that &quot;unbelivable&quot; for example) with a Perception + Alertness (difficulty 6) check, <i>then</i> they only could escape if someone else saves them</div> </div> </div> </div>The unbelievability clause doesn't apply, since it states the victim just does, and this is a direct mind assault: the illusion only causes this particular effect on one target.<br /> <br /> It's a hallucination, the problem is that a regular illusion disappears upon disbelief, but <b>Horrid Reality</b> remains. Imagine yourself seeing a hole open in the ground and a demon claw out of it, it's clearly impossible, but you rub your eyes, pinch yourself, and it's still there. You're not drunk, you're not sleepy, your mind is clear, yet there's the hole and there's the demon, and all your senses agree.<br /> <br /> No. You don't need it to be believable. It just is, and nothing for now can convince your brain on the contrary. The line and whole description are very clear on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}